    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"show_code_link()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"bddc47dd\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 4. Building a Filtered Query\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The GDELT query is a single text string. We combine three things with spaces, which GDELT treats as \\\"all of these must be true\\\":\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. the keyword, in quotes, for an exact-phrase match (for example `\\\"direct air capture\\\"`)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. `sourcelang:eng` if English filtering is on\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. `sourcecountry:US` if US-source filtering is on\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The function below assembles that string from the settings in Section 3. Building the query in one small, testable function keeps the filtering logic in a single place.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 5,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"678d76be\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"Example query sent to GDELT:\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  \\\"direct air capture\\\" sourcelang:eng sourcecountry:US\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def build_query(keyword, english=FILTER_ENGLISH, us_source=FILTER_US_SOURCE):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Assemble the GDELT query string with optional language and country filters.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Example output: '\\\"direct air capture\\\" sourcelang:eng sourcecountry:US'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    parts = [f'\\\"{keyword}\\\"']            # exact-phrase match\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if english:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        parts.append(\\\"sourcelang:eng\\\")  # English-language sources only\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if us_source:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        parts.append(\\\"sourcecountry:US\\\")  # US-based outlets only\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return \\\" \\\".join(parts)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Show what the query looks like for one keyword\\n\",\n",
    "    \"example = build_query(\\\"direct air capture\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Example query sent to GDELT:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\" \\\", example)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"5a60e257\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 5. The Retrieval Function\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This function sends one request to GDELT for one keyword over one time window and returns the list of articles.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Key points, explained:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`startdatetime` / `enddatetime`** tell GDELT the time window, formatted as `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS`.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`maxrecords=250`** asks for the most the API allows.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`sort=datedesc`** returns newest first.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`format=json`** asks for the machine-readable reply.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The **retry loop** tries again with a growing pause if the server is briefly busy (GDELT sometimes returns a temporary error under load). This makes the pull robust to transient hiccups.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The function returns a plain list of article records; it does not yet clean or store them.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 6,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"5624702f\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"DOC_API = \\\"https://api.gdeltproject.org/api/v2/doc/doc\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def fetch_window(query, start, end, retries=4, pause=5.0):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fetch up to 250 articles for one query over [start, end).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    query : the filtered query string from build_query()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    start, end : datetime objects marking the time window\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Returns a list of article dictionaries (empty list on failure).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    params = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"query\\\": query,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"mode\\\": \\\"ArtList\\\",                 # return a list of articles\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"maxrecords\\\": 250,                 # the API maximum\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"sort\\\": \\\"datedesc\\\",                # newest first\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"format\\\": \\\"json\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"startdatetime\\\": start.strftime(\\\"%Y%m%d%H%M%S\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"enddatetime\\\": end.strftime(\\\"%Y%m%d%H%M%S\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    url = DOC_API + \\\"?\\\" + urlencode(params)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for attempt in range(retries):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        try:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            reply = requests.get(url, headers=USER_AGENT, timeout=60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            # A valid reply is JSON beginning with '{'\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            if reply.status_code == 200 and reply.text.strip().startswith(\\\"{\\\"):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                return reply.json().get(\\\"articles\\\", [])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        except requests.RequestException:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            pass                            # network error; will retry\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        time.sleep(pause * (attempt + 1))   # wait longer each retry\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return []                               # give up quietly after retries\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"3d137005\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 6. Working Around the Record Limit (Time Chunking)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Because GDELT returns at most 250 articles per request, a busy keyword over a long period would be cut off. The fix is to split the date range into **monthly windows** and fetch each separately, then combine. A single month rarely exceeds 250 articles for a niche topic, so this recovers the full coverage.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The helper below turns a start and end date into a list of monthly windows.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 7,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"0653307c\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"The date range splits into 132 monthly windows:\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  2015-01-01 to 2015-02-01\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  2015-02-01 to 2015-03-01\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  2015-03-01 to 2015-04-01\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  ...\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def month_windows(start_date, end_date):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Yield (window_start, window_end) pairs, one per calendar month.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    current = start_date\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    while current < end_date:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # find the first day of the next month\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if current.month == 12:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            nxt = current.replace(year=current.year + 1, month=1, day=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            nxt = current.replace(month=current.month + 1, day=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        yield current, min(nxt, end_date)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        current = nxt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Preview the windows for the configured range\\n\",\n",
    "    \"windows = list(month_windows(START_DATE, END_DATE))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"The date range splits into {len(windows)} monthly windows:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for w_start, w_end in windows[:3]:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  {w_start.date()} to {w_end.date()}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"  ...\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"47fcd915\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 7. Running the Retrieval (Looping Over Every Search Term)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This is the step that loops over your search terms. The `retrieve_all` function below walks through **every keyword** in `KEYWORD_PAIRS` (built from `TECH_DICT` in Section 3), and for each keyword loops over every monthly window. So adding a term to `TECH_DICT` automatically includes it here - there is nothing else to change.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Two useful options are built in:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`save_per_keyword=True`** writes a small raw CSV for each keyword as it finishes, into a `raw_by_keyword/` folder. If a long run is interrupted, you keep everything already collected and can resume. This is the safe way to run a big pull.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- The combined raw results are returned as one table, which we then save whole in the next cell.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This cell talks to the internet and may take several minutes. If `LIVE_DISPLAY` is on, it refreshes a small dashboard in place as it runs - a bar chart of counts by family, the top keywords so far, and the newest rows as a table - so you watch the corpus build live. If off, it prints a plain progress line per keyword instead. Either way it ends with a summary. The `REQUEST_DELAY` pause keeps the load on GDELT's free server courteous. (Live display refreshes only when run interactively in Jupyter; a static HTML export captures the final frame.)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
