    "     \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"execute_result\"\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def save_raw(df, label=\\\"gdelt_climate_news_RAW\\\"):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Save the untouched raw results to a timestamped CSV.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    span = f\\\"{START_DATE:%Y%m%d}_{END_DATE:%Y%m%d}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    filters = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if FILTER_ENGLISH:   filters.append(\\\"eng\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if FILTER_US_SOURCE: filters.append(\\\"us\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    tag = \\\"_\\\".join(filters) if filters else \\\"all\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    path = f\\\"{label}_{tag}_{span}.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df.to_csv(path, index=False, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Saved RAW: {len(df)} rows to {path}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"save_raw(raw_df)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"e21eec67\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 8. Reconciliation and Quality Checks\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Before cleaning, this section checks that the pull behaved as expected. It answers three questions:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. **How does this run compare to a previous one?** Paste old per-keyword counts into `OLD_COUNTS` to see a side-by-side with the difference.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. **Did any keyword hit the 250 record ceiling in a single month?** Because we fetch one month at a time, the 250 cap now applies *per month*. If any keyword-month returns exactly 250, that month was likely truncated and you are missing articles - the fix is to fetch that keyword in shorter windows (for example weekly).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. **Did the filters actually take?** It lists the languages and source countries present. With `sourcelang:eng` and `sourcecountry:US` on, you should see only English and only United States. Anything else means a filter did not apply.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Run this after retrieval and read the flags. It changes no data - it only reports.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": 10,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"2357e292\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [\n",
    "    {\n",
    "     \"name\": \"stdout\",\n",
    "     \"output_type\": \"stream\",\n",
    "     \"text\": [\n",
    "      \"============================================================\\n\",\n",
    "      \"RECONCILIATION AND QUALITY CHECKS\\n\",\n",
    "      \"============================================================\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  keyword                              new   old   delta\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  ------------------------------------------------------\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  ocean alkalinity enhancement         103\\n\",\n",
    "      \"\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  --- Truncation check (any month at the 250 cap) ---\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  OK: no single month hit the cap; monthly chunking is sufficient.\\n\",\n",
    "      \"\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  --- Filter adherence ---\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  languages present : {'English': 103}\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  OK: English-only held.\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  countries present : {'United States': 103}\\n\",\n",
    "      \"  OK: US-source-only held.\\n\",\n",
    "      \"============================================================\\n\"\n",
    "     ]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# --- Optional: paste per-keyword counts from a previous run to compare ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# (These are the numbers from the earlier proof-of-concept run. Edit freely.)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"OLD_COUNTS = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"solar geoengineering\\\": 117,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"solar radiation management\\\": 27,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"stratospheric aerosol injection\\\": 72,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"marine cloud brightening\\\": 31,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"cirrus cloud thinning\\\": 3,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"direct air capture\\\": 230,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"CAP = 250   # the DOC API per-request record ceiling\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def reconcile(raw_df, old_counts=None, cap=CAP):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"RECONCILIATION AND QUALITY CHECKS\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if raw_df.empty:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(\\\"  raw_df is empty - nothing to check.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # 1. Per-keyword totals for this run\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    new_counts = raw_df.groupby(\\\"keyword\\\").size().to_dict()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # 2. Per-(keyword, month) counts, to detect single-month truncation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    tmp = raw_df.copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    tmp[\\\"month\\\"] = pd.to_datetime(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        tmp[\\\"seendate\\\"], format=\\\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\\\", errors=\\\"coerce\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ).dt.to_period(\\\"M\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    window_counts = tmp.groupby([\\\"keyword\\\", \\\"month\\\"]).size()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    truncated = window_counts[window_counts >= cap]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # 3. Per-keyword table, with old comparison if provided\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    header = f\\\"  {'keyword':<34}{'new':>6}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if old_counts:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        header += f\\\"{'old':>6}{'delta':>8}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(header)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"  \\\" + \\\"-\\\" * (len(header) - 2))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for kw in sorted(new_counts, key=lambda k: -new_counts[k]):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        line = f\\\"  {kw:<34}{new_counts[kw]:>6}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if old_counts and kw in old_counts:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            delta = new_counts[kw] - old_counts[kw]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            line += f\\\"{old_counts[kw]:>6}{delta:>+8}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(line)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # 4. Truncation flag\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"\\\\n  --- Truncation check (any month at the {} cap) ---\\\".format(cap))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if len(truncated):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(\\\"  WARNING: these keyword-months hit the cap and may be cut off:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        for (kw, mo), n in truncated.items():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            print(f\\\"    {kw} / {mo}: {n}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(\\\"  -> re-fetch these keywords in shorter (weekly) windows.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(\\\"  OK: no single month hit the cap; monthly chunking is sufficient.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # 5. Filter adherence\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"\\\\n  --- Filter adherence ---\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    langs = raw_df[\\\"language\\\"].value_counts().to_dict()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  languages present : {langs}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    non_en = {k: v for k, v in langs.items()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"              if k and k.lower() not in (\\\"english\\\", \\\"eng\\\")}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"  \\\" + (\\\"OK: English-only held.\\\" if not non_en\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                  else f\\\"WARNING: non-English present -> {non_en}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    countries = raw_df[\\\"country\\\"].value_counts().to_dict()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  countries present : {countries}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    non_us = {k: v for k, v in countries.items()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"              if k and k.upper() not in (\\\"US\\\", \\\"UNITED STATES\\\")}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"  \\\" + (\\\"OK: US-source-only held.\\\" if not non_us\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                  else f\\\"NOTE: non-US present -> {non_us}\\\"))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"reconcile(raw_df, OLD_COUNTS)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"8888ff50\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 9. Cleaning and Deduplication\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"News wire stories are often reprinted by many outlets, so the same headline can appear many times. We keep the **earliest** copy of each and record how many duplicates existed, so corpus size is reported honestly (raw counts overstate coverage).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Steps:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Drop rows with an empty link or headline.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Convert `seendate` to a proper date so we can sort by time.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Collapse duplicate headlines, keeping the earliest, and add a `dup_count` column.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"21133e2b\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def clean_and_dedupe(df):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Clean the raw results and remove duplicate headlines (keep earliest).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df = df.copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # 1. Drop rows missing a link or a headline\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df = df[(df[\\\"url\\\"].str.strip() != \\\"\\\") & (df[\\\"title\\\"].str.strip() != \\\"\\\")]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # 2. Parse the GDELT date (format: 20260115T143000Z) into a real datetime\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df[\\\"date_parsed\\\"] = pd.to_datetime(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        df[\\\"seendate\\\"], format=\\\"%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ\\\", errors=\\\"coerce\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df = df.sort_values(\\\"date_parsed\\\", na_position=\\\"last\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # 3. Normalize the headline for duplicate detection\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df[\\\"title_key\\\"] = (df[\\\"title\\\"].str.lower()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                       .str.replace(r\\\"[^a-z0-9 ]\\\", \\\" \\\", regex=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                       .str.replace(r\\\"\\\\s+\\\", \\\" \\\", regex=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                       .str.strip())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # count copies, then keep the earliest of each\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df[\\\"dup_count\\\"] = df.groupby(\\\"title_key\\\")[\\\"url\\\"].transform(\\\"size\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df = df.drop_duplicates(\\\"title_key\\\", keep=\\\"first\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df = df.drop(columns=[\\\"title_key\\\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return df\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"clean_start = time.time()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"clean_df = clean_and_dedupe(raw_df)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"CLEANING SUMMARY\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  raw rows in         : {len(raw_df)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  clean rows out      : {len(clean_df)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  removed (dupe/empty): {len(raw_df) - len(clean_df)}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      f\\\"  ({100*(len(raw_df)-len(clean_df))/max(len(raw_df),1):.1f}%)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if len(clean_df):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  unique titles       : {clean_df['title'].nunique()}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  by family           : {dict(clean_df['domain'].value_counts())}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  with country filled : {int((clean_df['country'].str.strip() != '').sum())}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"          f\\\" of {len(clean_df)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    most_dupes = clean_df.nlargest(3, 'dup_count')[['keyword', 'dup_count', 'title']]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  most-syndicated headlines (copies seen):\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for _, r in most_dupes.iterrows():\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"    {r['dup_count']:>3}x  {r['title'][:50]}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  cleaning time       : {format_seconds(time.time() - clean_start)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"clean_df[[\\\"domain\\\", \\\"keyword\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"country\\\", \\\"date_parsed\\\"]].head()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"09b0462b\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Save the cleaned results\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Now save the cleaned, deduplicated table as its own CSV, separate from the raw file. You now have two files: the raw pull (everything GDELT returned) and the cleaned corpus (one row per unique article). Downstream sentiment scoring uses the cleaned file.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"6e461626\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def save_clean(df, label=\\\"gdelt_climate_news_CLEAN\\\"):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Save the cleaned, deduplicated results to a timestamped CSV.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    span = f\\\"{START_DATE:%Y%m%d}_{END_DATE:%Y%m%d}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    filters = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if FILTER_ENGLISH:   filters.append(\\\"eng\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if FILTER_US_SOURCE: filters.append(\\\"us\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    tag = \\\"_\\\".join(filters) if filters else \\\"all\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    path = f\\\"{label}_{tag}_{span}.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df.to_csv(path, index=False, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Saved CLEAN: {len(df)} rows to {path}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"save_clean(clean_df)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"32430cee\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 10. Scraping the Article Body Text\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"GDELT gives you the headline and the link, but **not the article body**. If you want full-text sentiment (not just headline sentiment), you fetch each article's text from its URL. This section does that.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**What web scraping is:** downloading a web page and extracting the readable article text from it, stripping away menus, ads, and navigation. We use two libraries:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **trafilatura** (primary) - a well-regarded article-text extractor (Barbaresi, 2021).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **newspaper3k** (fallback) - tried if trafilatura returns nothing.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Being a good citizen.** The function honors each site's `robots.txt` (the file where a site states what automated tools may access), pauses between requests, and records a status for every article so you know what succeeded. Some articles will fail: paywalls, dead links, and login walls are normal, especially for older URLs. Those rows keep an empty body and a status code explaining why.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Install the libraries once with: `pip install trafilatura newspaper3k`\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"385df0ae\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# pip install trafilatura newspaper3k     # <- run once if not installed\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from urllib.parse import urlsplit\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from urllib.robotparser import RobotFileParser\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"_robots_cache = {}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def _allowed(url):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Check the site's robots.txt to see if fetching this URL is permitted.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    host = urlsplit(url).netloc\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if host not in _robots_cache:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        rp = RobotFileParser(f\\\"https://{host}/robots.txt\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        try:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            rp.read()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        except Exception:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            rp = None                      # no robots.txt reachable; allow\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        _robots_cache[host] = rp\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    rp = _robots_cache[host]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return True if rp is None else rp.can_fetch(\\\"*\\\", url)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def fetch_body(url):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return (body_text, status) for one article URL.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    status is one of: ok, ok_fallback, robots_disallowed, fetch_failed.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    import trafilatura\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if not _allowed(url):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return \\\"\\\", \\\"robots_disallowed\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    try:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        html = trafilatura.fetch_url(url)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if html:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            text = trafilatura.extract(html, favor_precision=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            if text:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                return text, \\\"ok\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # fallback to newspaper3k\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        from newspaper import Article\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        art = Article(url)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        art.download(); art.parse()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if art.text:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            return art.text, \\\"ok_fallback\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    except Exception:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        pass\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return \\\"\\\", \\\"fetch_failed\\\"\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"29755528\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Run the body scrape\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The cell below adds two columns to the cleaned table: `body` (the article text) and `fetch_status` (what happened). \\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Start small.** Scraping is slow (about 1-2 seconds per article) and hits real websites, so the `LIMIT` below runs only the first 25 articles as a test. Set `LIMIT = None` to scrape the whole corpus once you are happy it works. Expect this to take roughly one second per article plus the polite delay.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"88c49a3e\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"from collections import Counter\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"BODY_DELAY = 1.0        # seconds between article fetches\\n\",\n",
    "    \"LIMIT = 25              # scrape only the first 25 as a test; set None for all\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def add_bodies(df, limit=LIMIT, delay=BODY_DELAY):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fetch body text for each article; add body and fetch_status columns.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    Prints running progress, success/fail counts, timing, and an ETA.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df = df.copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    subset = df.head(limit) if limit else df\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    n = len(subset)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"SCRAPING BODY TEXT for {n} articles\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"          f\\\"{' (LIMIT set; increase to scrape all)' if limit else ''}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    run_start = time.time()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    bodies, statuses = [], []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    status_counts = Counter()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for i, url in enumerate(subset[\\\"url\\\"], 1):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        text, status = fetch_body(url)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        bodies.append(text)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        statuses.append(status)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        status_counts[status] += 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        # progress every 5 articles: counts, timing, ETA\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if i % 5 == 0 or i == n:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            elapsed = time.time() - run_start\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            rate = elapsed / i\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            eta = rate * (n - i)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            ok = status_counts[\\\"ok\\\"] + status_counts[\\\"ok_fallback\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            print(f\\\"  [{i:>4}/{n}] ok {ok:>4} | \\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                  f\\\"failed {status_counts['fetch_failed']:>4} | \\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                  f\\\"blocked {status_counts['robots_disallowed']:>3} | \\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                  f\\\"elapsed {format_seconds(elapsed)} | ETA {format_seconds(eta)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        time.sleep(delay)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    subset = subset.copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    subset[\\\"body\\\"] = bodies\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    subset[\\\"fetch_status\\\"] = statuses\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    total_time = time.time() - run_start\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ok = status_counts[\\\"ok\\\"] + status_counts[\\\"ok_fallback\\\"]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"SCRAPING COMPLETE\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  attempted          : {n}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  succeeded          : {ok}  ({100*ok/max(n,1):.0f}%)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  failed             : {status_counts['fetch_failed']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  blocked by robots  : {status_counts['robots_disallowed']}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  total time         : {format_seconds(total_time)}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  seconds / article  : {total_time/max(n,1):.1f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if ok:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        lengths = [len(b) for b in bodies if b]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"  median body length : {int(sorted(lengths)[len(lengths)//2])} chars\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"=\\\" * 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return subset\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"bodies_df = add_bodies(clean_df)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"bodies_df[[\\\"keyword\\\", \\\"title\\\", \\\"fetch_status\\\"]].head()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"669e4afe\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Save the corpus with body text\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Save the version that includes the scraped bodies as a third CSV. You now have three files: RAW (everything GDELT returned), CLEAN (deduplicated metadata), and WITH_BODY (cleaned plus article text). Body text can be large, so this file will be bigger than the others.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"1d45dfe8\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def save_with_body(df, label=\\\"gdelt_climate_news_WITH_BODY\\\"):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Save the cleaned corpus with scraped body text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    span = f\\\"{START_DATE:%Y%m%d}_{END_DATE:%Y%m%d}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    filters = []\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if FILTER_ENGLISH:   filters.append(\\\"eng\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if FILTER_US_SOURCE: filters.append(\\\"us\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    tag = \\\"_\\\".join(filters) if filters else \\\"all\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    path = f\\\"{label}_{tag}_{span}.csv\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df.to_csv(path, index=False, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Saved WITH_BODY: {len(df)} rows to {path}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return path\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"save_with_body(bodies_df)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"82bbaea8\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 11. Optional: Sentiment and Volume Over Time (Triangulation)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Besides article lists, the DOC API can return GDELT's own summaries of a topic, which are useful as an independent cross-check against sentiment you compute yourself later:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`mode=TimelineVol`** - how much coverage a term received over time (its share of global news).\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **`mode=TimelineTone`** - the average tone of that coverage over time.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"These are optional. They give a GDELT-computed sentiment-and-attention signal you can compare against your own scores, strengthening a methods chapter. The function below fetches one such timeline for one keyword.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"92a2183f\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def fetch_timeline(keyword, mode=\\\"TimelineTone\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                   start=START_DATE, end=END_DATE):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Fetch a GDELT timeline (TimelineTone or TimelineVol) for one keyword.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    params = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"query\\\": build_query(keyword),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"mode\\\": mode,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"format\\\": \\\"json\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"startdatetime\\\": start.strftime(\\\"%Y%m%d%H%M%S\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        \\\"enddatetime\\\": end.strftime(\\\"%Y%m%d%H%M%S\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    }\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    url = DOC_API + \\\"?\\\" + urlencode(params)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    try:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        reply = requests.get(url, headers=USER_AGENT, timeout=60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        if reply.status_code == 200 and reply.text.strip().startswith(\\\"{\\\"):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            return reply.json()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    except requests.RequestException:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        pass\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return {}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Example (uncomment to run):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# tone_timeline = fetch_timeline(\\\"direct air capture\\\", mode=\\\"TimelineTone\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# print(json.dumps(tone_timeline, indent=1)[:500])\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"879279cd\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 12. Limitations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"An honest record of what this pipeline does and does not capture:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Source country filtering is strict.** `sourcecountry:US` excludes US outlets whose country GDELT could not resolve, so it undercounts. Restricting to US sources also changes the population from global anglophone coverage to US-outlet coverage - a scoping decision to state in the methods and, for a confirmatory study, to preregister.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Relevance ranking and the 250 cap.** Even with monthly chunking, an extremely high-volume month could exceed 250 articles and be truncated; narrow the window further if a keyword saturates.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Recent coverage bias.** The DOC API is most reliable from about 2017 onward. Older corpora need GDELT's bulk files.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Headlines, not full text.** This pipeline collects headlines and metadata. Article bodies must be fetched separately from each URL if full-text sentiment is required.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Document-level tone.** GDELT's own tone (if used via the timelines) is computed for the whole document and cannot isolate sentiment toward a specific technology.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"6b2e1f4f\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 13. References and Resources\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Cited works** (DOIs verified against Crossref, July 2026):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
