    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 14. Export This Notebook as a Shareable HTML Report\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"This turns the notebook, with all its printed output, tables, and figures, into a single self-contained HTML file you can open in any browser or email to a collaborator.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Important distinction:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **Live updating** (the dashboard in Section 7) happens only while you run the notebook in Jupyter, because live updating needs Python running behind it.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **The HTML export** is a *snapshot*: it freezes whatever outputs exist at export time into a static file. Run the notebook fully first, then export, so the figures and tables are populated in the snapshot.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Two ways to export, below: a quick in-notebook command that saves an HTML file locally, and a note on committing it to GitHub once your repository is set up.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c63719c0\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"import subprocess\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import datetime as dt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Option 1: save the HTML report locally, next to your data.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# This runs nbconvert on THIS notebook file. Set the notebook filename\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# to match what you saved it as.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"NOTEBOOK_FILENAME = \\\"GDELT_climate_news_retrieval_documented.ipynb\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"LOCAL_REPORT_DIR = CODE_PATH_LOCAL + \\\"/gdelt/reports\\\"   # change if you like\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"def export_html(notebook=NOTEBOOK_FILENAME, out_dir=LOCAL_REPORT_DIR):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Export this notebook to a self-contained HTML report saved locally.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    import os\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    stamp = dt.datetime.now().strftime(\\\"%Y%m%d\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    out_name = f\\\"gdelt_retrieval_report_{stamp}\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    cmd = [\\\"jupyter\\\", \\\"nbconvert\\\", \\\"--to\\\", \\\"html\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"           \\\"--output-dir\\\", out_dir, \\\"--output\\\", out_name, notebook]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Running:\\\", \\\" \\\".join(cmd))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if result.returncode == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(f\\\"Saved HTML report to: {out_dir}/{out_name}.html\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        print(\\\"Export failed:\\\\n\\\", result.stderr[-500:])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Uncomment to run after you have executed the whole notebook:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# export_html()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"c092b263\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Option 2: publish the report to GitHub\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Once your GitHub repository is set up, you can share the HTML report so anyone can view it:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Save the notebook and export the HTML with the cell above.\\n\",\n",
